<title>UK: Cobham unit wins 20 mln stg RAF contracts.</title>
<headline>Cobham unit wins 20 mln stg RAF contracts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>FR Aviation, a firm controlled by the Cobham Plc group, said its joint venture FRA Serco had been awarded two contracts to manage facilities of Royal Air Force bases in the UK worth over 20 million stg.</p>
<p>In a statement, FR Aviation said the contracts was for a period of five years.</p>
<p>The first contract is at the Brize Norton air base in Oxfordshire and starts on March 13, 1997. The other contract is at Cosford, in the West Midlands, which will start on March 1, 1997, the statement added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
